-- title:
--   Igusa-type valuation subrings: discreteness and chart-algebra localisation
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime, $M'$ a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$.
--
--   **Base data.** $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and the hypothesis `hι` asks for a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is, by `hH₁`, the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$; thus $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ both modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. The intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ is, by `hK`, [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension of scalars `coeffEmb`, of the field of $q$-expansions over $\mathbb{Q}$ of modular functions for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   $A$ is a discrete valuation ring which is a domain with fraction field $L$, henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, and $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. The hypotheses on $A$ are: $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`), $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), $\mathfrak{m}_A = (\varpi)$ (`hϖ`), and a tame element $\varpi_t \in A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). The element $j \in K$ is non-zero and its Laurent series is `coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq` (`hj`), the $j$-series $\mathsf{q}^{-1} + \dots$. Write $C := \mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ for the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, $X := \mathtt{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$ for the pushout scheme of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two chart algebras along the middle chart, and $X_{\mathrm{fin}} := \operatorname{Spec} C$ with its map $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ to $X$.
--
--   **Supersingular maximal ideal.** $y \subseteq C$ is a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) at which $j$ is supersingular (`hss`): for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld-chart witness hypothesis `hArig`.** For every point $z$ of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}(y') = z$ at which the above supersingularity condition holds for $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there exist: a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v - f\,u)$, satisfying seven clauses (summarised here): (i) $e$ sends the germ of each $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) each $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and each $L$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ which is a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ — `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`, namely: for every ratio of modular forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions representing an element $x$ of $K$ and every embedding $\iota$ of $L$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, the Laurent series of $\tau x$ read through $\iota$ is the corresponding ratio of the $q$-expansions of the two forms translated by the matrix `conjElemN q γ⁻¹` — maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$ then the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ transporting the completed germ map along $\tau$, a constant $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ fixing constants, $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; (v) two primes of $S$ containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, not containing both $X_0$ and $X_1$, and containing linear forms $a_iX_0+b_iX_1$ up to order two with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions along $e$ composed with the completion map; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, not containing both $X_0, X_1$, and containing $X_0$ up to order two, and for $a \in C$: the completed germ of $a$ lies in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and, after subtracting a suitable $a_0 \in A$ so as to lie in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, its image under $e$ composed with the completion map is the class of some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0 \ge 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ form $\sum_i \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b \in W$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   **A fixed witness.** A point $z$ of $X$ with the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ in $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}_{X,z}}$ (`hϖz`, `hz`), a point $y'$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ over $z$ (`hy'`) satisfying supersingularity (`hss'`) and with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`), together with data $W_1, \sigma_1, \mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, $f_1, u_1, v_1$ (units $u_1,v_1$; $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$) and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk with $S_1 := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$ are fixed, and `hW₁` asserts for these data exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) listed above.
--
--   **Blow-up data.** $J \subseteq C$ is, by `hJ`, the infimum of the ideals obtained as follows: for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, take the contraction along $e_1$ composed with the completion and germ maps of the ideal of $S_1$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t), X_0, X_1$, and pull it back along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$. The $A$-subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ is, by `hB`, generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$.
--
--   **The valuation subring $W$ and its properties.** $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hR1` states that $C \le B$ and that every element of $K$ is a ratio of two elements of $B$ with non-zero denominator. The hypothesis `hR2` states that $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. The hypothesis `hR3` (five clauses) states that $W$ meets $L$ exactly in the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b \in C$ membership in $y$ is equivalent to $b$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, and that $W$ is the set of ratios $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$. The hypothesis `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) states: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to \mathtt{DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing}\,q\,k$ whose vanishing locus is $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$, compatible with $A \to k$, and equivariant in the sense that for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ there is $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathtt{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) such that $\rho \circ \tau = \mathtt{hAction}\,(\mathtt{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c) \circ \rho$ on $B$, with $c \neq 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; that $\Gamma_0(M')$-level automorphisms preserve $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is hit by the image under some $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$-level automorphism of $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$; that an element of $B$ all of whose images under such automorphisms lie in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a $\Gamma_0(M')$-level automorphism preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses, for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ such that (a) for $x \in L$ the image of $x$ in $K$ lies in $V$ if and only if $x$ lies in the image of $A$, (b) the image of $\varpi$ lies in $V$ and in $\mathfrak{m}_V$, (c) every element of $C$ lies in $V$, and (d) there exists $c \in C$ such that for every monic polynomial $p \in A[T]$ the value at $c$ of the image of $p$ in $K[T]$ lies in $V$ and is not in $\mathfrak{m}_V$, the following two assertions hold: $V$ is a discrete valuation ring; and for every $f \in K$, $f$ lies in $V$ if and only if there are $g,h \in C$ with $h \in V$ a unit of $V$ and $f\,h = g$.
--
--   The conclusion is thus a statement about an arbitrary valuation subring $V$ subject to (a)–(d), and presents $V$ as a localisation of the $j$-finite chart algebra $C$, not of $B$.
--
--   This is the Igusa-type local analysis at a supersingular point of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over a henselian discrete valuation ring $A$: it identifies every valuation subring of the function field lying over $A$, integral on the $j$-chart and generic in the required sense, as a discrete valuation ring which is the localisation of the $j$-chart algebra at its centre. It is the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-diamond variant, valid without the restriction $q \ge 5$, and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_isPrime_forall_igusaType_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_isPrime_forall_igusaType_mem_maximalIdeal_iff_of_end_blowupChart_of_dvd) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.forall_mem_iff_map_mem_igusaValuation_of_isLevelAutAt_gamma_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.forall_mem_iff_map_mem_igusaValuation_of_isLevelAutAt_gamma_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_dvd).
